    "productType": "DAYTOUR",
    "name": "Bruny Island Small-Group Guided Tour ",
    "shortDescription": "Bruny Island, Oyster, Tasmanian ancient tales, Fridge Baker, South Bruny \r\n布魯尼島｜美味生蠔｜ 塔斯原住民｜窯烤麵包｜布魯尼島南島國家公園\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "description": "<h3 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><b><u><br></u></b></h3><h3 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><b><u>Bruny Island Day Tour</u></b></h3><p><br></p><p><b><br></b></p><p><b>Duration: 8 hrs</b></p><p><b><u><br></u></b></p><h4 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"></h4><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">This is a remarkable opportunity to explore untamed nature and completely immerse yourself in breathtaking landscapes. Tasmania boasts an incredible array of biodiversity, with ancient forests and pristine oceans that have thrived for millions of years. Our tours provide an intimate outdoor experience, allowing you to reconnect with nature through leisurely walks on the stunning Bruny Island. Tasmania offers a truly wild and invigorating environment—why not experience it firsthand and breathe in the crisp, fresh air?</span><p><br></p><p><b><u>What To Expect:</u></b></p><p>·&nbsp;<span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">&nbsp;The views from Truganini Lookout.</span></p><p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">·&nbsp; Experience enchanted South Bruny National Park</span></p><p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;Get Shucked Oyster</span></p><p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;Bruny Island Cheese and Beer Co.</span></p><p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">·&nbsp; Rare opportunities for Wildlife Encounter</span></p><h4><br></h4><h3 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><p><b><br></b></p><p><b>**Pick up**</b></p><p><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Princes Wharf No. 1, Castray Esplanade, Hobart</span></u><br><br></p></h3><h4><b><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"><br></span></u></b></h4><h4><b><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Itinerary:</span></u></b></h4><p><b><u><br></u></b></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"></p><p><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Bruny Island Ferry</span></b><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">From Hobart to Bruny Island is about 45 minutes.</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">At the ferry terminal, we expect to hop on the ferry with a mini-bus and have</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">about 15-20 minutes of travel time.</span><br><br><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Get Shucked/ Bruny Island Oyster</span></b><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Enjoy the taste of the beautiful local oysters and fresh produce.</span><br><br><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Bruny Island Cheese Company</span></b><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Warm shop offering locally produced craft cheeses, beers &amp; bread, with tastings &amp; picnic</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">tables.</span><br><br><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">The Neck</span></b><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">There may be 200&nbsp;stairs to climb, but the views are definitely worth it. The Neck Lookout</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">gives you a bird's eye view of the spectacular natural landscape of North and South Bruny Island.</span><br><br><b>South Bruny National Park</b><br><br>South Bruny National Park’s towering cliffs are a spectacle set against the wild Southern Ocean. Atop one of the southern headlands is Cape Bruny Lighthouse, first lit in 1838 and today offering a fascinating insight into the history of this rugged coastline. Nearby Cloudy Bay is popular with surfers and ideal for long walks on the beach. You may even find yourself watching southern right and humpback whales on their annual migration as you explore the beaches and headlands of South Bruny.<br><br></p><p><b>Lunawanna Cafe</b><br><br>The Lunawanna Cafe, serving great coffee and food in a whimsical setting, celebrates the extraordinary beauty and rich natural diversity of Bruny Island. A cafe at the southernmost end of an island, off an island, off an island. Next stop, the South Pole! Make your last resort your first choice. A feast for both the eyes and the stomach.<br><br><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Adventure Bay</span></b></p><p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Adventure Bay Bruny Island is known for its</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">beautiful 7km long, east-facing beach. It has a sheltered feel with many large</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">gum trees surrounding the beach and the cliffs of Fluted Cape on the southern</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">end. It’s got a relaxed Australian beach town feel, and unlike many of these</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">towns, it’s managed to keep this vibe without becoming commercialized. Explore</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Island's wild animals such as Echidna, White Wallabies, Quolls, etc.</span><br><br><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Bruny Island Honey</span></b><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">The Honey Pot and</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Bruny Island Honey is the houses of honey venue of the Wright family’s</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">proudly run lifelong collaboration between our family, the bees, and the</span><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Tasmanian Wilderness.</span><br><br><br><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">North Bruny Ferry</span></b><br><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">Drive to the Ferry terminal for departure and back to the starting point.</span><br></p><p></p><h4><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\"><br></span></u></h4><h4><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">What is included:</span></u></h4><h3 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><p>Air-con Bus ｜Guided Tour｜Professional photography x1</p><p></p><p><b><u><br></u></b></p><p><b><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-medium\">What is Not Included:</span></u></b></p><p>Lunch｜Personal Expense ｜Travel Insurance</p><p><br></p></h3><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"></p><p><br></p><p><a><b>**Pick Up Point**✨</b><br><b>Prices Wharf to Tasman Peninsula / Bruny Island</b><br><b>Princes Wharf No. 1, Castray Esplanade, Hobart</b></a></p><b><i>**Tour starts from 0830 a.m.** ///</i></b><b><i>**Hotel Pick-Up is available**&nbsp;</i></b><p><b><u><br></u></b></p><h3><u><br></u></h3><h3><u><br></u></h3><h3><u>探索布魯尼島之旅</u></h3><p></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"></p><p><b><u>行程介紹</u></b><b><u>:</u></b></p><p>布魯尼島（Bruny Island）位於澳大利亞塔斯馬尼亞州南部，是該州最受歡迎的自然旅遊勝地之一。島上擁有塔斯馬尼亞一些最壯觀的海岸線，包括壯麗的懸崖、清澈的海灘以及豐富的野生動植物。布魯尼島實際上由北布魯尼和南布魯尼兩個部分組成，通過一個狹窄的地峽「頸部」連接起來。「頸部」不僅提供了絕佳的觀景點，可以俯瞰整個島嶼的美景，還是島上觀察企鵝的理想場所。南布魯尼國家公園內分布著許多最壯麗的景觀，吸引了大量徒步旅行者、鳥類愛好者和探險者。</p><p>除了令人驚嘆的自然美景，布魯尼島的本地特產也同樣引人入勝。這裡的生產商專門生產高品質的生蠔、奶酪、蜂蜜、威士忌和巧克力，讓遊客在探索自然之美的同時，也能享受美食的樂趣。布魯尼島不僅是大自然愛好者的天堂，也是美食愛好者的理想之地，展現了塔斯馬尼亞的多樣魅力。</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b><u>行程特色:&nbsp;</u></b></p><p>● 華語/英語 導遊與您一起深入探險大自然風光</p><p>● 島嶼風情體驗 /島上原住民歷史</p><p>● 參觀 布魯尼島南端 國家公園風景</p><p>&nbsp;● 有機會觀賞當地野生動物(白色袋鼠)與原生自種植物</p><p>&nbsp;● 享受島嶼生蠔與當地美酒天然的結合</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b><u>行程包含</u></b><b><u>:</u></b></p><p>國家公園入園證/ 空調冷氣小巴士/ 戶外嚮導帶領</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b><u>行程不包含</u></b><b><u>:</u></b></p><p>中餐/ 各人消費/ 旅遊保險</p><p></p><h3 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><b><u><br></u></b></h3><h3 class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><p><a><b>**集合地點**✨</b><br><b>Prices Wharf to Tasman Peninsula / Bruny Island</b><br><b>Princes Wharf No. 1, Castray Esplanade, Hobart</b></a></p><b><i>**行程出發時間 0830 a.m.** ///</i></b><b><i>**荷巴特飯店接駁OK**&nbsp;</i></b></h3>",
